> I just purchased a USB flash drive so that I can play the same Nethack
> at home and work.  ASCII Nethack works just fine, but when I try to
> load the tiled version I get a message that says "Cannot load tiles
> from the file.  Reverting back to default."  The line in default.nh is
> as follows:
> OPTIONS=tile_file:absurd64.bmp,tile_height:64,tile_width:64
> 
> As you can see there is no drive letter indicating where the files
> live, so I just assumed it would load out of the hack directory.
> Anyone have any ideas?

Perhaps it is trying to run them from the "current" directory. Try setting
the current directory at the command prompt:

C:> F:
F:> CD Nethack
F:\Nethack> Nethackw.exe

Alternatively, try specifying a complete path in the options value:

OPTIONS=tile_file:F:\Nethack\absurd64.bmp,tile_height:64,tile_width:64

